th the new  administration  over the border in brownsville texas we  met up with one of the moms in this  group who says they crossed the river  on a raft paying a smuggler 800 dollars  for two people  they asked for asylum when they were  picked up by border patrol  that process begins with a cova test and  a negative result  means they are released into the united  states to wait for a hearing  andrea rudnick is with team brownsville  a grassroots organization working to  help families gain asylum  they're just choosing at this point not  to even go through the process  that's right because because the word  has gotten out  that families with young children are  getting across and getting released to  go on to those families  i mean it's catch and release all over  again yes it is  we're trying not to use those words but  yes it is while the administration  and congress work through legislation  and mexican officials say they don't  have the resources to care for families  like this  anymore people like rudnick and her  organization  are left trying to fill the gaps for  team brownsville  our motto has always been meeting the  needs  one family at a time and that's really  all i can think about i can't think  about  ten thousand people a hundred thousand  people a million people  today just 25 people will be allowed to  cross this border and finish out their  asylum cases in the u.s and that number  is expected to grow  over the next few weeks but just to  point out the trump administration did  believe  catch and release didn't work because  families wouldn't show up to court but  there is  evidence that shows up to 96 percent of  the families that are requesting asylum  do show up to their court hearings gail  maria thank you very much
 

